cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pulse-ep-decay in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "pulse-ep-decay: Geodesic spatial-resolution analysis for intracardiac pace-mapping"
abstract: >-
  Python package for quantifying the spatial resolution of scalar fields
  (e.g., pace-mapping matching scores) on triangulated atrial surface meshes.
  Geodesic distances are computed with the Heat Method (Crane et al. 2017),
  and a Gaussian-decay model is fit to the radial score profile; the resulting
  width parameter sigma serves as a physical-unit (millimetre) resolution
  measure. Includes a synthetic validation framework that recovers known
  sigma from generated score fields and reports bias statistics. The
  scientific kernel works on any triangulated mesh and scalar field; an
  optional adapter integrates with the pulse-ep CARTO platform.
